    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Three ways in which the lives of farmers and herders would have been different from hunter-gatherers are: • Hunt-gatherers keep moving from place to place in search of food while farmers and herders grow their food from their living place. • Hunt-gatherers did not build any permanent houses mostly they live in caves while farmers and herders build huts and houses. • Hunt-gatherers had no role in protecting animals and plants while farmers and herders protect animals and plants.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, farmers and herders have a more settled lifestyle compared to hunter-gatherers.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
